-- title:
--   The trace of a finite field extension as a sum of Frobenius powers
-- statement:
--   **The field trace of $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}/\mathbb{F}_p$ is the sum of the Frobenius conjugates.**
--
--   Let $p$ be prime, $n \ge 1$, and let $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$ be the Galois field with $p^n$ elements.
--   The extension $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}/\mathbb{F}_p$ is Galois with cyclic Galois group generated by
--   the Frobenius automorphism $\varphi(x) = x^{p}$. For every $x \in \mathbb{F}_{p^n}$,
--
--   $$\operatorname{Tr}_{\mathbb{F}_{p^n}/\mathbb{F}_p}(x)
--   \;=\; x + x^{p} + x^{p^{2}} + \cdots + x^{p^{n-1}}
--   \;=\; \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} x^{p^{i}},$$
--
--   the identity holding in $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$ after embedding the trace, which a priori lies in
--   $\mathbb{F}_p$.
--
--   This is the concrete form of the general fact that for a finite Galois extension the trace is
--   the sum over the Galois group, $\operatorname{Tr}(x) = \sum_{\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}}\sigma(x)$,
--   specialised to the cyclic group $\langle\varphi\rangle$ of order $n$.
--
--   Its practical importance is that it turns the trace — defined abstractly as the trace of the
--   $\mathbb{F}_p$-linear multiplication-by-$x$ map — into an explicit **polynomial** expression.
--   That is what makes the additive characters $\psi(x) = e^{2\pi i\,\mathrm{Tr}(x)/p}$ of a finite
--   field computable, and hence underlies the treatment of Gauss, Kloosterman and other exponential
--   sums over $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$.
--
--   **Formalization note.** The left-hand side applies `algebraMap` to move
--   `Algebra.trace (ZMod p) (GaloisField p n) x` from $\mathbb{F}_p$ into $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$, so
--   both sides live in the larger field. The hypothesis $n \ne 0$ ensures the extension is
--   non-degenerate.
-- source:
--   Classical; see Lidl & Niederreiter, *Finite Fields*, Theorem 2.23, and Lang, *Algebra*, Ch. VI. Lean proof extracted from `Salt/Weil/Kloosterman.lean` of the Salt project, https://github.com/jyh/salt (Apache-2.0, Jason Hickey).

import Mathlib

namespace FiniteFields

theorem galoisField_trace_eq_sum_frobenius (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (n : ℕ) (h : n ≠ 0)
    (x : GaloisField p n) :
    algebraMap (ZMod p) (GaloisField p n) (Algebra.trace (ZMod p) (GaloisField p n) x)
      = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range n, x ^ (p ^ i) := by sorry

end FiniteFields
